# Vercel serves whatever it receives, unauthenticated, at rmtrackerchatgpt.vercel.app.
# The GitHub repository is private; the deployment is not. So everything that is not
# needed to render the page is kept out of the deployment rather than published at a
# guessable URL.
#
# The page needs exactly three files: index.html, data.json and access.json.
#
# dumps/ holds the operational Excel dumps — sales transactions, receivables ageing and
# customer contract prices. Publishing those would put commercial data on the open web,
# and contract prices are the reason the `mes` account is denied the SKU pricing tab in
# the first place.
dumps/

# The skill, its docs and the session memory belong in the repository, not on the site.
# All three now live under .claude/ — the project instructions, the session memory and
# the skill package, which carries the approved masters (zmat, the RM tracker model and
# the customer contract prices) under assets/masters/. One line covers them, and any
# future file added under .claude/ is covered by it too.
.claude/
.pytest_cache/
